<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2278"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is the Carol Mould case starting to look like a later BTK murder? The differences in MO and style could be accounted for by BTK&#39;s age and physical limitations as he gets older &#40;if he has any&#41;. What else stands out to anyone? I know that is seems we want to want to try to have  everything this side of the Lincoln assasination blamed on BTK, but this one starts to look more like it might be BTK. Lt. Landwher was at the scene when it occured and was assisting in the investigation. Lot of little things make me think maybe we are seeing the work of BTK in 2004. Lets PLEASE nail this guy!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
