<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3636"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe Gotcha has a point. Lately we seem to be willing to pin the Kennedy assasination on BTK as well as every unsolved midwestern murder since 1960 or so. As I continue to consider this one, Mrs. Mould&#39;s case does not seem to really fit BTK&#39;s signature.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
