<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3640"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 10:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are many interesting links and/or coincidences &#40;I don&#39;t believe in them&#41; regarding Carol Mould&#39;s Murder and someone close to it... Tom decided to delete most of the discussion. <BR> <BR>Interesting Fact: Her Husband is a Criminal Psychologist among other aspects of his career and frequently serves as an expert witness in Sedgwick County trials on psychological evaluations... He has a office within a stones throw of the Otero Home.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
