<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3913"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 7:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->FLAME ON! <BR>All I can say is that this thread has degenerated into the most ridiculous demonstration of ignorance and fantasy that has ever appeared on this message board.  The glaring errors and false assumtions trying to fit some of the facts of this case into the btk case are far too numerous to mention.  The &#39;evidence&#39; presented in the posts is even self-contradictory.  One example only:  the site listing the internship of the victim&#39;s husband is cited as suspicious due to the fact he did the internship a few blocks from Murdock park.  But if you look at the date for the internship, he finished it in 1980.  In what may be news for some, a professional does not START PRACTICING until they finish the internship.  Thus, this professional could not look into the windows of the Otero home because he did not have an office until 6 years after the Oteros were murdered. The  building in question is not &#39;a stones throw&#39; from the Oteros, it is blocks away, and can not be seen from the sidewalk in front of the Otero home. I know because I have stood on that sidewalk.  But it would not matter if you could, as btk was not this man&#39;s patient and looked into the Otero home from the roof of the building as the Oteros had been killed 6 years &#40;at least&#41; earlier. <BR>As Gotcha, said above, get a grip.  If you can. <BR>Flame out!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3913-->
<!--Post: 3925--><!--Time: 1105417734-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3925"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jabez<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jabez<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oklahoma_mike, do you have any opinions on what did happen to Carol Mould? <BR> <BR>Just to note-during an internship, though they may not have their own practice, interns do go out into the field and shadow with a doctor.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3925-->
<!--Post: 3926--><!--Time: 1105417827-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK watched the manhunt and heard the wailing sirens from the comfort of his nearby palatial home, located in the rather exclusive section of Wichita known as Arrowhead Heights. Sorry, I couldn&#39;t resist. I agree with Oklahoma Mike completely.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
