<!--Post: 3942--><!--Time: 1105429997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3942"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 11:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mrs. Mould seems to have been killed in an impulsive crime, maybe a burglury gone bad, ora rape attempt in which sghe fought back and the perp killed her.  The attempt at burning seems to have been planned after the fact with what was in the home, using gasoline to cover her body and pour a trail out the door as a fuse.  The perp found another accelerant&#40;charcoal lighter, paint thinner, whatever&#41; and used it in another part of the house.  Perp was inexperienced, maybe first murder and panicked in ways to try and cover up the crime.  Probably a young perp who started something which got way out of hand.  That is my best guess, but I admit only a guess.  On to btk.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
