<!--Post: 3965--><!--Time: 1105477022-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3965"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 12:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Listen Flame...Mike... &#34;A stones throw is a &#34;relative term&#34; it is close and I for one never said he had to have the office there in 1974. <BR> <BR>Pardon the pun... Easy Killa... <BR> <BR>&#34;professional could not look into the windows of the Otero home&#34; <BR> <BR>As I already said: I&#39;m not accusing or assuming that he is guilty of anything. <BR> <BR>&#34;as btk was not this man&#39;s patient&#34; <BR> <BR>OK... you know it all Bud. <BR> <BR> <BR>BTW: You stood in front of their house... to do what?.. and you tell someone else to get a grip... go get &#39;em Sooner.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3965-->
<!--Post: 3967--><!--Time: 1105478570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3967"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 1:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some similarity to the Barbera A. Smith murder <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.wichitasedgwickcountycrimestoppers.com/unsolved_murders/" target=_top>http://www.wichitasedgwickcountycrimestoppers.com/ unsolved_murders/</a> <BR> <BR>The Murder of Barbara Smith &#40;1980&#41; <BR>On October 25, 1980 the body of Barbara Smith, a 37-year old white female, was discovered by her husband and daughter at their home at 1151 S. Waverly. Barbara had been murdered by severe blunt force trauma to her head. The killer had also tried to burn down the house but was unsuccessful. Her family last saw Barbara alive on October 24, 1980. Police reports indicate that there were no signs of forced entry to Barbara’s home. The type and amount of force used make police suspect the killer was someone who may have known Barbara. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3967-->
<!--Post: 3968--><!--Time: 1105479183-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3968"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 1:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems like I&#39;ve heard this scenario many times.  Like Mould and Smith, where the victim&#39;s been murdered and the murderer attempted to cover the crime up with a fire.  As Mike mentioned, it seems very impulsive, like in a moment of panic and makes me think a murder was never the goal, but perhaps a rape or robbery and things got out of hand. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
