<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4066"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 7:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The only ones that jumped out at me from this article were Dolores Davis, Marine Hedge, and the Slaughter couple. <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_c" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_c</a> ourts/8411738.htm  <BR> <BR>Does anyone think it likely that he would sexually assault his victims? I think his actions &#40;a million opportunities to do so, yet choosing against it&#41; illustrate his inability to have intercourse directly with his victims. Maybe that&#39;s changed, who knows. And the three named above grabbed my attention because of the ages of the victims. I believe its highly likely that he&#39;s progressively choosing older victims. I&#39;m not sure why I feel so strongly about that. Re: the fires, I think his desperate need for recognition suggests that he wouldn&#39;t want to cover up his &#34;work&#34; with a fire. I could be wrong. <BR> <BR>BTW To Nadeltanz on your Jan. 6 post: LexisNexis is a legal research system. It&#39;s private access-password required, and used by law students registered through school or lawyers who pay a lot of $ for its use. I don&#39;t think it would help your research anyway, as it mostly contains law review articles, statutes and criminal/civil opinions published by state and fed courts. <BR>If, for some reason, you do want to look up laws or court case opinions, try <a href="http://www.findlaw.com" target=_top>www.findlaw.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
