<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5565"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 10:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sheriff Craig Murphy also said right after the above statement that they have not ruled out &#34;anyone&#34; at this point... in the death of Carol Mould. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m interested in this case in particular... I haven&#39;t heard back from Tom on this but he said to an emailer once: <BR> <BR>&#34;I&#39;ve heard from several sources that someone close to Mould was considered a BTK suspect long before her death.&#34; <BR> <BR>In response to:  <BR> <BR>&#34;Subject: Carol Mould <BR>A relative of Carol Mould was questioned as a BTK suspect years ago....&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/mail.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/mail.html</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>That emailer went on to say that although Carol Mould&#39;s purse was recovered her drivers license was still missing. <BR> <BR>I remember reading that &#34;what&#34; was missing was found... Does that mean the purse and &#34;all&#34; of it&#39;s contents? <BR> <BR>The Sherriff also made mention of traveling to Iowa to speak to some &#34;interesting individuals&#34;. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5565-->
