<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6469"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nadeltanz<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nadeltanz<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Q I am trying to answer your 2 questions, but am not making myself clear. My first post re your <BR>first question was deleted. I said in that post that the Joseph Otero/S.Killett on the map you <BR>were referring to, comes from the address on the first postcard dated Jan. 25 and supposedly from <BR>B. is written as follows: S.Killett 803 Edgemore as the return address for said postcard. When I got back to you later, you must have already found <BR>the answer to the how the connection went down between the names S.Killett and Joseph Otero on your own. I &#34;say again&#34; that post to you was deleted. I see that my second one to you has not been deleted. In the second post, I was too brief. the point I was trying to make is that for every marker on the map their is an individual&#39;s name corresponding to the marker e.g. Nancy Fox\marker.Marine Hedge\marker, sorry I&#39;m not sure if Marine Hedge was on the map, I don&#39;t have the map in front of me.  And Q this is repeated with every proper name: First Name\Last Name\Marker. Therefore, and I hope I have not confused my point,Therefore, the names on the map of Joseph Otero\S.Killett would be following the same pattern as all the proper names. It&#39;s just a pattern. Now I guess Analyzer could have put in the Otero&#39;s\S. Killett or he could have put all the names of the members of the Otero&#39;s who were victimized, but I personally cannot remember all their names except for Josephine and that comes for being able to rememeber Joseph. I apologize to the living Otero son for not remembering his name, as I have recently seen him interviewed on AMW. So, basically I&#39;m trying to say that Analyzer was trying to save time and space by letting the name Joseph stand for the whole Otero Family. A &#34;big word&#34; for this is &#34;synecdoche&#34; meaning for example &#34;all 50 sails cast off their mooring lines and set sail&#34;. Sails as a part of the whole. Joesph Otero representing the Otero family. I&#39;m sure Analyzer wanted to save some time and work by choosing Joseph Otero to represent the entire Otero family. No, I don&#39;t think you&#39;re being rude Q. On the contrary. <BR>Nadeltanz 2/7/05  11:05 <BR>P.S. Just to make sure: I am answering <BR>your question: &#34;why did you single out Joseph Otero&#34;. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
