<!--Post: 6556--><!--Time: 1107887163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6556"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 10:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well Tom if you&#39;ll indulge me just one more post to Nadeltanz, it had to do with one of A&#39;s maps with Carol Mould as just one of the marked locals... thin but I just want to say to Nadeltanz: <BR> <BR>I understand your point but was asking Analyzer. The including of &#34;S. Killett&#34; seems out of place and why not just sau &#34;Oteros&#34;? <BR> <BR>Some of these maps were also posted as links in chat by someone calling themselves &#34;dreamer&#34;.  <BR> <BR>At the time no mention of Carol Mould was even involved in chat and a map of A&#39;s type was linked to that showed &#34;only&#34; a green line to the Mould residense. Odd considering it was out of the blue, so to speak. I&#39;ve already asked A about it and got a reply. <BR> <BR>My  other 2 questions to &#34;Analyzer&#34; still stand. <BR> <BR>Please, although I know your trying to be helpful, let A answer, as A is the one who made the map&#40;s&#41;. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
